---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Blog — Praweg Koirala"
  description="Thoughts on software engineering, AI, cloud computing, and building products."
>
  <h1 class="mb-2 text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em]">Blog</h1>
  <p class="mb-8 text-lg text-muted">Thoughts on building, coding, and the cloud.</p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8">
    <article class="rounded-md border border-line bg-card p-8 transition duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:shadow-lg hover:shadow-accent/10">
      <time class="mb-2 block text-sm text-muted" datetime="2026-09-01">September 1, 2026</time>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold">
        <a href="/blog/hello-world" class="text-fg no-underline transition-colors hover:text-accent">Hello, World — New Site, New Stack</a>
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-4 text-muted">Rebuilding prawegko.dev with Astro, deployed on S3/CloudFront with OIDC CI/CD. Here's the stack and why I chose it.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1">
        <span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-accent/12 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-sm font-medium text-accent">Meta</span>
        <span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-accent/12 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-sm font-medium text-accent">Astro</span>
        <span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-accent/12 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-sm font-medium text-accent">AWS</span>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
